From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: fix RTL8261C firmware probe

rtl8261c_cg_probe() first calls rtl826x_probe(), which selects and requests
either rtl8261n.bin or rtl8264b.bin based on the vendor version register.
It only requests rtl8261c.bin after that generic probe succeeds.

Systems shipping only the firmware required by their RTL8261C therefore
keep deferring the Realtek driver probe and eventually bind the Generic
Clause 45 PHY driver.  Besides skipping the RTL8261C initialization, that
driver can report an incorrect negotiated link speed.

Pass the model-specific firmware initializer into the common probe path.
The RTL8261C then loads only rtl8261c.bin while existing RTL826x users keep
their current firmware selection.

Ported to the 25.12 (6.12) version of the RTL826x support.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2204,7 +2204,8 @@ static int rtl826x_patch_db_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 		return rtl8264b_phy_patch_db_init(phydev);
 }
 
-static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
+static int rtl826x_probe_with_patch(struct phy_device *phydev,
+				    int (*patch_db_init)(struct phy_device *))
 {
 	struct device *dev = &phydev->mdio.dev;
 	struct rtl826x_priv *priv;
@@ -2225,7 +2226,7 @@ static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	 */
 	phydev->eee_broken_modes |= MDIO_EEE_100TX | MDIO_EEE_1000T;
 
-	ret = rtl826x_patch_db_init(phydev);
+	ret = patch_db_init(phydev);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -2235,6 +2236,11 @@ static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	return rtl826x_probe_with_patch(phydev, rtl826x_patch_db_init);
+}
+
 /* 6.12 predates phy-common-props (v7.0). These are the two helpers
  * rtl826x_config_serdes_polarity() needs, carried locally, together with
  * the PHY_POL_* values from dt-bindings/phy/phy.h.
@@ -2380,11 +2386,8 @@ static int rtl8261c_cg_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = rtl826x_probe(phydev);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return ret;
-
-	ret = rtl8261c_phy_patch_db_init(phydev);
+	ret = rtl826x_probe_with_patch(phydev,
+				       rtl8261c_phy_patch_db_init);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
